// =====================================================================
// Pulse — Flow v1.5 third-genre showcase (EDM)
// =====================================================================
// The v1.5 closer artifact (SHOWCASE-01, D-11/D-13). Sits alongside
// v1.4's classical *symphony* (examples/showcase.flow) and the jazz
// *ragtime/markov* generative piece (examples/generative/markov_jazz.flow)
// to prove Flow's genre-agnostic claim across three contrasting genres.
//
// Genre: EDM (four-on-the-floor, sidechained pad, granular riser).
// Duration: ~60s of looped material (8 four-bar sections @ 128 BPM).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// FIVE-PRIMITIVE FEATURE CHECKLIST (SHOWCASE-01) — where each appears:
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
//   1. Phase 35 pattern matching  — `(match ...)` over the section index
//      drives bassline variation (see `bassFor` below, line ~70).
//   2. Phase 36 generative        — SEEDED `(euclidean 7 16 ... seed)`
//      kick/clap rhythm (line ~60). Seed makes it byte-identical.
//   3. Phase 37 granular DSP       — `(granular ... )` riser texture on
//      the rendered build-up (line ~110).
//   4. Phase 38 live block         — `live 1bar { ... }` hot-swap loop
//      (DEMO section, commented out — line ~150).
//   5. Phase 40 real-time MIDI     — `midiOut(song, port)` over @midi
//      (DEMO section, commented out — line ~160).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// RENDER / DEMO SPLIT (Pitfall 5, D-v1.5-07):
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// The file has TWO sections:
//
//   (A) PINNED OFFLINE RENDER — everything down to the `writeWav` +
//       `writeMidi` calls. Every stochastic call here carries an EXPLICIT
//       SEED, so the PrngRegistry reseeds at the writeWav boundary and two
//       consecutive renders produce byte-identical WAV+MIDI. This is the
//       section pinned by `scripts/test_two_run_determinism.sh` and the
//       `Phase41ShowcaseRmsTests` RMS-windowed regression (±0.5 dB/100 ms,
//       SPEC-8). NO `live` block, NO real-time `midiOut`, NO unseeded PRNG
//       in this path.
//
//   (B) LIVE / REAL-TIME DEMO — a `live 1bar { ... }` hot-swap block and a
//       `use "@midi"` + `midiOut(song, port)` real-time MIDI demonstration.
//       Both opt OUT of the determinism contract (D-v1.5-07): the live block
//       re-evaluates on file save, and real-time MIDI needs librtmidi + a
//       hardware port. They are COMMENTED OUT so a headless `flow render`
//       never blocks on the live loop or stalls on absent MIDI hardware —
//       uncomment and run under `flow watch` / a real rig to hear them.
//
// Render (offline, deterministic):
//   dotnet run --project flow-cli -- run examples/edm/pulse.flow
//   → /tmp/pulse.wav + /tmp/pulse.mid
//
//   The writeWav/writeMidi targets below are absolute (/tmp/...) so the
//   determinism harness — which runs the script with an arbitrary CWD —
//   resolves them identically from any directory (same convention as
//   examples/generative/markov_jazz.flow). Copy /tmp/pulse.wav elsewhere
//   to keep it.
//
// Determinism check (exits 0 = byte-identical across two renders):
//   bash scripts/test_two_run_determinism.sh examples/edm/pulse.flow \
//     --render-cmd "dotnet run --project flow-cli -- render <SCRIPT> -o <OUT>"
// =====================================================================

use "@std"
use "@audio"
use "@patterns"
use "@generative"

// =====================================================================
// (A) PINNED OFFLINE RENDER — seeded, deterministic.
// =====================================================================

tempo 128 {
    timesig 4/4 {
        key Aminor {

            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            // 1. SEEDED generative rhythm (Phase 36).
            //    `(euclidean hits steps note humanize jitter seed)` —
            //    a 7-in-16 four-on-the-floor-adjacent kick pattern and a
            //    sparser 4-in-16 clap. Explicit seeds (1305 / 808) make the
            //    humanized output byte-identical across renders (PrngRegistry
            //    reseeds at the writeWav boundary per D-v1.5-06).
            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            Sequence kick = (euclidean 7 16 A1 0.12 0.06 1305)
            Sequence clap = (euclidean 4 16 D3 0.10 0.05 808)

            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            // 2. PATTERN MATCHING (Phase 35).
            //    `(match idx | 0 => ... | _ => ...)` selects a bassline
            //    motif per section index — verse / build / drop variation
            //    without an if-ladder. The match is resolved EAGERLY here
            //    (statement-block-free) so the active key context applies.
            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            Sequence bassVerse = | A1q A1q E2q A1q |
            Sequence bassBuild = | A1e A1e E2e A1e C2e A1e E2e G2e |
            Sequence bassDrop  = | A1q E2q G2q A1q |

            // Resolve the per-section bass via pattern matching on the index.
            Sequence b0 = (match 0 | 0 => bassVerse | 1 => bassBuild | _ => bassDrop)
            Sequence b1 = (match 1 | 0 => bassVerse | 1 => bassBuild | _ => bassDrop)
            Sequence b2 = (match 2 | 0 => bassVerse | 1 => bassBuild | _ => bassDrop)

            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            // 3. @patterns combinator (Phase 36, bonus) — `fast` doubles the
            //    drop bassline for the final section's energy lift. Cycle
            //    unit = bars (D-36-04); no PRNG, fully deterministic.
            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            Sequence bDropFast = (fast b2 2.0)

            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            // Pad bed — sustained Am / F / C / G outlined as whole notes.
            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            Sequence pad = | A3w | F3w | C4w | G3w |

            // Lead arp riff for the drop.
            Sequence lead = | A4e C5e E5e A5e G5e E5e C5e A4e |

            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            // Arrange the ~60s piece: 8 four-bar sections @ 128 BPM ≈ 60s.
            // verse → verse → build → DROP → DROP → build → verse → out.
            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            section verse {
                Sequence groove = kick
                Sequence snap = clap
                Sequence low = b0
                Sequence bed = pad
            }
            section build {
                Sequence groove = kick
                Sequence snap = clap
                Sequence low = b1
                Sequence bed = pad
            }
            section drop {
                Sequence groove = kick
                Sequence snap = clap
                Sequence low = bDropFast
                Sequence bed = pad
                Sequence top = lead
            }
            section outro {
                Sequence bed = pad
            }

            Song song = [verse verse build drop drop build verse outro]

            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            // Render the song to a Buffer, then shape it with the EDM
            // effects chain: lowpass tighten → sidechain-style compression
            // pumped against the kick energy → reverb tail → delay slap.
            // All effects are deterministic DSP (no PRNG).
            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            Buffer rawMix = (renderSong song "saw")
            Buffer tight = rawMix -> (lowpass 8kHz)
            Buffer pumped = (compress tight -12dB 4.0 5ms 120ms)
            Buffer spaced = pumped -> (reverb 0.4 1.6s)
            Buffer slapped = spaced -> (delay 250ms 0.35 0.3)

            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            // 4. GRANULAR DSP (Phase 37) — a granular riser texture layered
            //    under the mix. Source is a short sine swell; granular pulls
            //    grain-sized chunks (Hann window) and overlap-adds them into
            //    a cloud. The jitter PRNG routes through PrngRegistry and
            //    reseeds at the writeWav boundary → byte-identical.
            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            Buffer swell = (createSineTone 2.0s 220Hz 0.35)
            Buffer riser = (granular swell 60ms 18Hz 0.4)
            Buffer riserWet = (reverb riser 0.6)

            // Final mix: pumped EDM body + granular riser, trimmed to avoid clip.
            Buffer body = (mix slapped riserWet)
            Buffer finalMix = (volume body 0.8)

            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            // PINNED OUTPUTS — both deterministic.
            //   WAV: seeded render path → two-run cmp-clean (SPEC-8 RMS pin)
            //   MIDI: writeMidi → DryWetMidi, structurally deterministic
            // -------------------------------------------------------------
            (writeWav "/tmp/pulse.wav" finalMix)
            (writeMidi "/tmp/pulse.mid" song)
        }
    }
}

// =====================================================================
// (B) LIVE / REAL-TIME DEMO — NOT pinned, opts OUT of determinism.
//     (D-v1.5-07 / Pitfall 5). Commented out so a headless `flow render`
//     never blocks on the live loop or stalls on absent MIDI hardware.
//     Uncomment ONE block at a time to drive the interactive features.
// =====================================================================
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// 4. LIVE BLOCK (Phase 38) — hot-swap loop under `flow watch`:
//      dotnet run --project flow-interpreter -- --watch examples/edm/pulse.flow
//    Edit the `Sequence stab = | ... |` line and SAVE — the new content
//    swaps in at the next bar boundary with a 64-sample equal-power
//    crossfade. Emits `[live] entering live block ...` to stderr on entry
//    (D-v1.5-07: live mode opts OUT of two-run cmp-clean — by design).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// tempo 128 {
//     timesig 4/4 {
//         key Aminor {
//             live 1bar {
//                 section jam {
//                     Sequence stab = | A4e E5e A5e E5e A4e E5e A5e E5e |
//                 }
//                 Song loop = [jam]
//                 Buffer out = (renderSong loop "saw")
//                 (play out)
//             }
//         }
//     }
// }
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// 5. REAL-TIME MIDI (Phase 40) — stream the drop section to a hardware
//    synth / DAW track over ALSA-seq (needs librtmidi + an output port;
//    absent → charitable NullMidiBackend, never throws). `midiOut` reuses
//    the Phase 28 writeMidi GM prefix-match routing VERBATIM, so the port
//    sounds identical to the exported pulse.mid. Discover ports first:
//      (midiPorts)
//    then send (replace the port name with one from midiPorts):
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// use "@midi"
//
// tempo 128 {
//     timesig 4/4 {
//         key Aminor {
//             section drop {
//                 Sequence low = | A1q E2q G2q A1q |
//             }
//             Song stream = [drop]
//             midiOut(stream, "Your MIDI Port 0")
//         }
//     }
// }
